{"name":"Funhouse","hex":"#f3d9dc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"funhouse","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A structure, usually at a circus or amusement park, enclosing several interactive attractions such as distorting mirrors, ramps, slides, stairs, rotating barrel slides, etc., that usually do not involve performers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/funhouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Funhouse","blocks":[{"text":"A funhouse or fun house is an attraction found in amusement parks and funfair midways, equipped with various devices designed to surprise, challenge, or amuse visitors. Unlike thrill rides or dark rides, fun houses are participatory attractions where visitors enter and move around at their own pace. Incorporating aspects of an obstacle course, they seek to distort conventional perceptions and startle people with unpredictable physical circumstances."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Lost_City_-_Fun_House.jpg/330px-Lost_City_-_Fun_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funhouse","wikidata":"Q385589"},{"title":"Funhouse (Pink album)","blocks":[{"text":"Funhouse is the fifth studio album by American singer and songwriter Pink, released by LaFace Records and Jive Records in Europe on October 24, 2008, and on October 28 in the United States. A pop and pop rock record, Funhouse was inspired by Pink's separation from her husband, Carey Hart. To record the album, she enlisted her previous collaborators, such as Billy Mann, Butch Walker, Max Martin and MachoPsycho, while also involving new music producers and songwriters, such as Danja, Jimmy Harry, Tony Kanal and Eg White."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/86/Pinkfunhouse.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funhouse_(Pink_album)","wikidata":"Q166299"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/The_%27funhouse%27_ride_at_Malton_fair_-_geograph.org.uk_-_287501.jpg/500px-The_%27funhouse%27_ride_at_Malton_fair_-_geograph.org.uk_-_287501.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/The_%27funhouse%27_ride_at_Malton_fair_-_geograph.org.uk_-_287501.jpg/500px-The_%27funhouse%27_ride_at_Malton_fair_-_geograph.org.uk_-_287501.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The funhouse at Malton fair. The entire building folds onto one trailer for hauling.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_'funhouse'_ride_at_Malton_fair_-_geograph.org.uk_-_287501.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Illuminated_funny_house_at_Linnanm%C3%A4ki.jpg/500px-Illuminated_funny_house_at_Linnanm%C3%A4ki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Illuminated_funny_house_at_Linnanm%C3%A4ki.jpg/1280px-Illuminated_funny_house_at_Linnanm%C3%A4ki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Illuminated_funny_house_at_Linnanm%C3%A4ki.jpg/500px-Illuminated_funny_house_at_Linnanm%C3%A4ki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pellen talo (literally \"House of Clown\"), an illuminated funhouse at the Linnanmäki amusement park in Helsinki, Finland, during the annual lights carnival of Linnanmäki","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIlluminated_funny_house_at_Linnanm%C3%A4ki.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colou